Somebody said "The Artist is greater than the Mystic, since he can explain
his Vision to others". I think the problem is that many visionaries
concentrate very much on their visions, and regard them as almost
self-evident since they are so well integrated in their own world-views.
This unfortunately makes them very hard to understand for anybody who does
not understand their world-view very well. 

This is not only a problem for visionaries, its also a major problem in
all human communication. Just look at the problems of explaining Uploading
to normal people. It makes a lot of sense to most of us on the list, but
to many people it often sounds completely absurd. Another case of
mis-matched world-views. What we need is a transhumanist Jules Verne. 

